# Open Brain — Restore rehearsal cron entry (Unraid host)
#
# INSTALLED 2026-06-11 (Entry 164, arch-review v3 RC-2). Kept for reference/rebuild.
#
# INSTALL (once, after a homeserver rebuild):
#   1. SSH to homeserver as `root` (claude's passwordless sudo does NOT cover
#      tee/cat; /boot/config is root-only readable).
#   2. Append the cron line below (with its comment) to:
#        /boot/config/plugins/dynamix/custom.cron
#      Unraid reads /boot/config/plugins/dynamix/*.cron on boot and merges them
#      into /etc/cron.d/root (same persistence path as the ingest cron).
#   3. Reload cron so the line takes effect without a reboot:
#        /usr/local/sbin/update_cron
#   4. Verify (NOT `crontab -l` — dynamix merges into /etc/cron.d/root):
#        grep restore-rehearsal /etc/cron.d/root
#
# SCHEDULE: Sunday 05:30 — after wiki-lint (0 5 * * 0) and before the
#   production week starts. Staggered per P16 cron-slot audit: 0 5 * * 0
#   is taken by wiki-lint; 30 5 * * 0 is the next available Sunday slot.
#   DO NOT change to 0 5 * * 0 — that slot is occupied.
#
# ROLLBACK:
#   Remove the line from /boot/config/plugins/dynamix/custom.cron and
#   run update_cron again (as root):
#     sed -i '/restore-rehearsal/d' /boot/config/plugins/dynamix/custom.cron
#     /usr/local/sbin/update_cron
#     grep restore-rehearsal /etc/cron.d/root  # should return nothing
#   Script can remain in repo — it makes no writes unless explicitly invoked.
#   Ephemeral container (open-brain-rehearsal-pg) uses --rm; no persistent state.
#
# LOGS: /var/log/open-brain-restore-rehearsal.log
#   Rotate manually with: : > /var/log/open-brain-restore-rehearsal.log
#   Or via logrotate — add to /etc/logrotate.d/ if log grows large.
#
# PUSHOVER: Pass notification (priority 0/normal) and fail notification
#   (priority 1/high) sent via scripts/lib/pushover-notify.sh.
#   Requires PUSHOVER_APP_TOKEN and PUSHOVER_USER_KEY in environment — cron's
#   env is bare, so the cron line wraps the script in `bash -c 'set -a;
#   . ./.env.secrets; set +a; ...'` to auto-export them at run time.
#   (Do NOT put the secrets in custom.cron itself — that copies them onto the
#   /boot flash drive.)

30 5 * * 0 cd /mnt/user/appdata/open-brain && bash -c 'set -a; . ./.env.secrets 2>/dev/null; set +a; bash scripts/restore-rehearsal.sh' >> /var/log/open-brain-restore-rehearsal.log 2>&1
